WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:04.492
Thirty to 40 million Americans

00:00:04.492 --> 00:00:06.690
grind their teeth at night.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:11.021
That's roughly 10% of the US population,

00:00:11.021 --> 00:00:13.040
and chronic teeth grinding can lead

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.573
to painful issues from tooth fractures

00:00:16.573 --> 00:00:19.625
to changes in facial appearance.

00:00:19.625 --> 00:00:21.370
But the worst part is

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.261
you could be a teeth grinder

00:00:23.261 --> 00:00:24.519
and not even know it.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:34.208
Every time a grinder gnashes
their back molars together,

00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:37.050
they exert as much as 200 pounds of

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.230
pressure per square inch.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.540
That's 10 times the force
you exert on your teeth

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.440
when you chew normally.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.310
This pressure can crack and fracture teeth

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:52.572
and eventually even wear
them down to stumps,

00:00:52.572 --> 00:00:55.930
which can then require
root canals, implants,

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.530
or dentures.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:00.820
But it's not just your
teeth that take a beating.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.410
If you suffer from chronic
grinding, also called

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.829
bruxism in the medical
community, you could be

00:01:06.829 --> 00:01:09.940
grinding your teeth for
up to 40 minutes for

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.118
every hour you're asleep.

00:01:12.118 --> 00:01:15.166
That's enough to cause
headaches and a sore jaw

00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:16.360
in the morning,

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.669
and if you keep it up night after night,

00:01:18.669 --> 00:01:22.340
it could permanently damage your jaw.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:26.110
Researchers estimate that
20% of teeth grinders

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:28.840
have symptoms of a painful jaw condition

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.830
called TMD.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.200
TMD affects the movement of your

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.510
temporomandibular joints.

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:38.990
These joints connect
your jaw to your skull,

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.650
helping you eat, chew, and talk.

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:45.380
But when you grind your teeth incessantly,

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.950
you can overwork these joints.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:51.675
One study found that when
these muscles work overtime,

00:01:51.675 --> 00:01:54.458
they become tender and enlarged,

00:01:54.458 --> 00:01:58.290
making your face look
more square and masculine.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.650
What's more, the sound
of grinding teeth could

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.520
be enough to damage your hearing.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.910
Researchers who examined
400 university students

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:11.130
found a strong correlation
between grinding

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.820
and tinnitus.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.980
Tinnitus is a hearing
condition that causes

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.080
ringing in your ears and
can lead to hearing loss.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:23.640
But perhaps the scariest
part of all of this,

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.290
unless your roommate
or a partner hears you

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:29.170
grinding your teeth at
night, you might not

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.054
even realize you're doing it

00:02:31.054 --> 00:02:34.160
until your dentist notices the damage.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:38.430
And chances are, you've
probably done it yourself.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:43.330
An estimated 85 to 90% of
the population will grind

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:46.355
or clench their teeth to some degree.

00:02:46.355 --> 00:02:49.747
And while there's no
simple cure for bruxism,

00:02:49.747 --> 00:02:52.240
there's still hope.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.843
A mouth guard, for instance,

00:02:53.843 --> 00:02:56.417
won't stop you from grinding altogether,

00:02:56.417 --> 00:02:58.198
but it will stop your molars

00:02:58.198 --> 00:03:01.245
from wearing your teeth down to stumps.

00:03:01.245 --> 00:03:04.050
And since grinding is
often caused by stress

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.210
and anxiety, some doctors
recommend counseling

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:10.182
and meditation.

00:03:10.182 --> 00:03:12.282
So maybe a solution

00:03:12.282 --> 00:03:14.098
to your teeth-grinding problem

00:03:14.098 --> 00:03:17.090
is a nice long vacation.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.280
Doesn't sound too bad, right?

